{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:19cf9f14a146605e83e268b880638a930b565904","text":"Retired unclaimed. It asks claude to review b86eeb8b, and codex's pre-audit then found two security defects in that head: the managed .git/chess directory is accepted even when group- or other-writable, and publishKey ignores failure to remove its linked temporary copy of the private key. The head must not be approved, so the request must not stand.\n\nIt also asked claude to rule on whether two race guards could stay unwitnessed. That was mine to get wrong: request 747adca9 names concurrent publication in its conditions, so the requester had already decided, and putting it to a reviewer was asking someone else to reopen a settled condition.\n\nRepair is claimed under af4459bc; a fresh head will carry fresh artifacts and a fresh review request."}